data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":270,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_023d05c3f562fdcd016acb987f03bc8193a94b9d42a9f7ec48","call_id":"call_fc8eea10db314595a2477ff23de6dd17","name":"write","arguments":"{\"path\":\"README.md\",\"content\":\"# Workboard\\n\\nRequires Node.js 22.22.1. No external dependencies or installation needed.\\n\\n## Run\\n\\n```sh\\nPORT=8080 DB_PATH=./data/workboard.sqlite npm start\\n```\\n\\nOpen `http://localhost:8080`. The server binds to `0.0.0.0`. Defaults are port 8080 and `data/workboard.sqlite`; reuse the database path to retain projects across restarts.\\n\\nHealth check: `GET /health` returns `{\\\"status\\\":\\\"ok\\\"}`.\\n\\n## Verify\\n\\n```sh\\nnpm test\\n```\\n\\nTests launch isolated servers and temporary SQLite databases, checking project creation, validation, ordering, HTML escaping, navigation markup, health, and persistence across process restarts.\\n\"}","status":"completed"}}

event: response.completed
data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":271,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_023d05c3f562fdcd016acb987ae4748193a2580cd1dc21da8c","object":"response","created_at":1791727739,"completed_at":1791727747,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<addendum>\nKeep changes focused and readable. Use clear names and avoid needless duplication. Verify the changed behavior with appropriate checks before submitting.\n</addendum>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_023d05c3f562fdcd016acb987c63bc819386da962f03720d40","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Refining chunk handling**\n\nI want to keep things simple and not overdo it. There could be a minor fix needed for splitting UTF-8 chunk names related to body buffers; while it's not absolutely necessary, I think it would be good to address. I should also consider implementing a stop test that halts on failure after the first attempt to avoid rare hangs. Overall, I think I’m in a good place with these ideas and need to update the README."}],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqy5h_whf8majUvP4mLFYFGASa3u2FrE_8aNnYCbs2ExUp36sP3ThClm8b9Gy8HpD831_9SX80o-Oq7U3BW6O4GRupPOQlGtEwL67ngV8UkNOZU59HNKkTi6hZdN8q6maFE_AFD-r7Jtl3XPa99sg5OUkJgdPcI4stxt_MsT6VlLS-GbthDPj3CDtui79UWZ7R0OgMEXxvj3-PqYezCGB0pmXdBLJVZOE8BUYIT9NT3EebftwJRs3y9Vp5jEa1Iu_3by4P_E137H2usGQHG7Klc9GPKSX6aFbS5mDa_zxyMMUvfLAp54DO4XymuR6JG_O9qu2_a8CPhGclEoiAfaTaB9S5kJg4NxlKLwJKXd3vxoeKbzKus1LySJ6OXV9D-FXlGU63AZU4fps3jiv2IztP2eGaNjplalkwD0EwajIBCn0kD9tPg_Wyo7BfN1yLnNedrA1xgsfPA92RqdQ4wLZFeNM5NUoU5dnIj24yUaQxpZtGLSc_pErCfN07WEBWiPZytiyMtsQJLLpmxszhCk9w0lnz2O5SugoRptvN8JUDGeDvHDFrzHJFERYQNSAhcKGoTVEnNZf_6nHlgWZVymHExDyKxggxyIjh0oFl_ETFtHJG--URLjH1HwjWLxAvuYjG4kIck3McprSPs_XMa11Lyfh7a2cmdh_ojiZ0Cb7jMx5TqfLCelgFDD_biknZabmp3omK4MjJ69aBEes9JJ4OkW51KaX9wS6v9cxneM2JJIzAqNAx1UPNpIgEPWyQHNAM5FRK06BVR6SPpMJ_mars8842lDvM6LgKiW-OOCAz247CKxK2qy2hdKnnl0iDwHa9r8EgBV6nP8VD2n8kgJza4cmVhXWI_dfjxOs6l-kZYs3eqjrUEktba1QvHRpUz6oKnbJ3d_vAAuDXDHsrsO2ww_loZa6NDoZFnrcDU22DZnnkg8dBqMMJSEq9ry0HAd1plrXSl7NQ7YmIoMWbfL5tABOrzPv-PJ39sFbvTS4CTys2zJWHDibNc6ERmRI4Z7j8fOZGuD1FF9lvDr4CqXCbWgYvjKUGcgRZOFE5qnLBhsCVtODzOGTkA1mr70aKEORNM-I3ezpswe3iohgAKsgEUoAHmzwOY5zyz1U3A3L_KLTrutuvvHnvqYTIBqeD6xWszP34zPvnsJ4GfXw0wzu0gJT24zMq3tifodiAsSHtj5fY7z_PEPWZeEka7mMDO8n-S5YIr6qHtkTnPzRDzy0rEC5xtu4MlZWBvV5xNVwTtCHHZ4K-VCUQXYNAsy6JmetMbqi-GOGkFCjVu5bmGUfocZjuR8-tK98X1vvmrMe3uNRPFJfo75isnZI-RGUstYpY9B-B3tiMaso1FR1G1L1ugBfHm7t5ek0kJbZHNHFzKoMdEGNkQvrUhKsk_42wUwscpDSyCZt9k1wQ-lvSogONNoiBy1yGa14d01etcqkF5CpDVqu3XCybtiglp5LH_dDuy7pdxmSRtSXtuFBGUkW5A3Kj0v65R9H2MRA77T2l8brBABBQDfEZ0uCHboIG6T4tOK0ZvJbVqtYG9n7ZAWt0lbVp_9RULG_dFpzKEaoL8MbtWsBjuhdd3ExINQJjkcmHB1QihJebW_w4qcBLLEbnVNnB4yBQ_ouzixWRcgCW4wjm-ptuANn73OZzEyy-nntm1FgangEKh8fHLiOpRLblcx9_t1Fyvj2yVQzZCurccY274hxSmvvKNVCSDcJEhzANPs6YIpLNmzm6vQilqC93n3cLOK9cdUCpn9feh4ZpGav19XcfiYuCmGGoN6DIFR8Xvf5KjHxK1viHwSrS-jbLJtHS0WzYCr0wMSBpN04HNlj_cokzbjSGIbn_qAh8as4iJ8mP8Nmo8CFYCRC9TYyPdOzn8hVKYoPD5pGGsNweLPQPPga3CZfI1F1-PlWoEy8_9SCKl3WFpZ9a7GTn1J911ALS4uTSRv3TnUkr3_5fkFdBST